      "## Position 1: Officer Branch Operations (Job ID: 18220)\n\n### Role Overview & Responsibilities\nThe **Officer Branch Operations** is an integral front-line banking role responsible for executing smooth transactional workflows, upholding service excellence, and enforcing compliance standards at Karachi branches:\n\n- **Customer Account Servicing:** Processing account opening requests in compliance with State Bank of Pakistan (SBP) KYC/AML regulatory standards.\n- **Transaction Processing:** Handling clearing instruments, outward/inward remittances (RTGS, PRISM, pay orders, demand drafts), and utility collection.\n- **Cash Oversight & Customer Support:** Assisting head cashiers in daily balancing, vault cash verification, customer query resolution, and counter turnaround time (TAT) management.\n- **Regulatory Record-Keeping:** Maintaining proper audit trails, transaction vouchers, and system day-end balancing reports in the Core Banking System.\n\n### Eligibility Criteria\n- **Education:** Minimum Bachelor’s degree (Graduation / 14–16 years) from an HEC-recognized institution. Graduates in Commerce (B.Com), Business Administration (BBA), Economics, or Banking & Finance are given preference.\n- **Experience:** Suitable for ambitious entry-level professionals and candidates with up to 2 years of general branch banking operations experience.\n- **Key Skills:** Sound knowledge of basic retail banking products, basic arithmetic precision, proficiency with MS Office, and courteous communication.",
