      "## Quick Facts & Active Meezan Bank Vacancies Table\n\n| POSITION TITLE | PRIMARY LOCATION | MINIMUM EDUCATION | REQUIRED EXPERIENCE | POSTED DATE | APPLICATION DEADLINE |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Operation Manager (OM)** | Multiple Cities / Nationwide | Bachelor's Degree | 5+ Years (Min 1 Yr as OM) | 16 Oct 2026 | **05 November 2026** |\n| **Senior Branch Services Officer** | Multiple Cities / Nationwide | Bachelor's Degree | 4+ Years (Min 1 Yr Supervisory) | 16 Oct 2026 | **05 November 2026** |\n| **Quality Assurance Analyst** | Karachi Head Office | Bachelor's / Master's | 2+ Years in QA / Operations | 15 Oct 2026 | **15 November 2026** |",
      "## Position 1: Operation Manager (OM) — Multiple Cities\n\n### Role Overview & Key Responsibilities\nThe **Operation Manager (OM)** holds primary operational stewardship of the branch, ensuring seamless customer service while mitigating operational risks:\n\n- **Branch Operational Supervision:** Exercising end-to-end supervision over daily counter operations, clearing, cash handling, and non-financial account requests.\n- **Regulatory & Shariah Compliance:** Enforcing strict compliance with State Bank of Pakistan regulations, Shariah governance frameworks, anti-money laundering controls, and internal banking SOPs.\n- **Risk Mitigation & Control:** Overseeing GL account reconciliations, balancing vault cash, managing audit preparedness, and minimizing operational errors or losses.\n- **Turnaround Time (TAT) & Service Quality:** Monitoring transaction speed, resolving escalated customer grievances, and coaching branch service teams.\n\n### Minimum Eligibility Benchmark\n- **Education:** Minimum Bachelor’s degree from an HEC-recognized university or chartered institute. Professional banking diplomas (JAIBP / AIBP) or Islamic finance certifications are strongly preferred.\n- **Experience:** Minimum 5 years of verified retail banking experience, including at least 1 full year serving in the capacity of an Operation Manager in a commercial bank.\n- **Core Competencies:** Comprehensive understanding of SBP Prudential Regulations, clearing mechanisms (NIFT/PRISM), customer due diligence, and team leadership.",
      "## Position 2: Senior Branch Services Officer (SBSO) — Multiple Cities\n\n### Role Overview & Key Responsibilities\nThe **Senior Branch Services Officer (SBSO)** serves as a vital supervisory anchor on the branch floor, bridging management oversight and frontline transactional desks:\n\n- **Supervisory Authorization:** Authorizing teller cash payments, account debits/credits, pay order issuances, stop-payment requests, and signature verifications within designated authorization limits.\n- **Clearing & Remittance Oversight:** Superintending outward and inward clearing cycles, local collections, Inter-Branch Transactions (IBT), and remittances.\n- **Operational Backup:** Functioning as the primary second-in-command to the Operation Manager, stepping into operational management during audits, inspections, or absences.\n- **Regulatory Returns & Reporting:** Preparing accurate daily, weekly, and monthly operational reports, SBP returns, and Head Office compliance reconciliations.\n\n### Minimum Eligibility Benchmark\n- **Education:** Minimum Bachelor’s degree from an HEC-recognized university.\n- **Experience:** Minimum 4 years of proven branch banking operations experience, with at least 1 year in a supervisory or authorization capacity.\n- **Skills Required:** Strong attention to detail, high analytical ability, proficiency in Core Banking Systems, and effective conflict-resolution skills.",
      "## Position 3: Quality Assurance Analyst — Karachi Head Office\n\n### Role Overview & Key Responsibilities\nStationed at Meezan Bank's Head Office in Karachi within the **Service Quality Department**, the **Quality Assurance Analyst** monitors and evaluates institutional service benchmarks across customer touchpoints:\n\n- **Audit & Evaluation Reviews:** Conducting systematic QA reviews of customer service interactions, digital touchpoints, and branch operations to detect compliance and service anomalies.\n- **Grievance Trend Analysis:** Analyzing customer complaint logs, turnaround delays, and root causes to identify systemic operational inefficiencies.\n- **Management Dashboards & Reporting:** Formulating detailed service quality dashboards, thematic audit summaries, and corrective action recommendations for senior management.\n- **Process Improvement:** Collaborating with Learning & Development and Branch Operations teams to redesign customer journeys and enhance brand loyalty.\n\n### Minimum Eligibility Benchmark\n- **Education:** Minimum Bachelor’s degree (Master’s preferred) from an HEC-recognized institute. Academic specialization or certifications in Islamic Finance provide an added advantage.\n- **Experience:** Minimum 2 years of relevant experience in Quality Assurance, Service Quality, Complaint Management, or Banking Operations.\n- **Skills Required:** Strong data analytical skills, advanced spreadsheet capability, objective audit mindset, and excellent written and verbal business communication.",
      "## Step-by-Step Official Application Guide\n\nMeezan Bank conducts all recruitment transparently through its official web recruitment portal. Follow this verified guide to apply:\n\n1. **Access the Careers Gateway:** Visit the official portal at [meezanbank.com/careers](https://www.meezanbank.com/careers/).\n2. **Browse Current Openings:** Locate **Operation Manager**, **Senior Branch Services Officer**, or **Quality Assurance Analyst**.\n3. **Authenticate / Register:** Log in with your registered Meezan candidate profile or create a new profile by providing your CNIC, email, and personal contact details.\n4. **Profile Completion:** Accurately enter your academic qualifications, employer history, specific banking role dates, and JAIBP / Shariah certifications.\n5. **CV Upload:** Attach an up-to-date curriculum vitae clearly detailing your supervisory tenure and branch operational responsibilities.\n6. **Final Submission:** Confirm your preferred branch location or city choice and submit your application before **05 November 2026** (for OM & SBSO) or **15 November 2026** (for QA Analyst).",
      "## Recruitment Safety Advisory\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> **Important Recruitment Integrity Notice:**\n> Meezan Bank Limited never charges any test fee, registration fee, or training deposit during the hiring process. Never share sensitive banking details or transfer funds to individuals claiming to represent Meezan Bank recruitment teams. Apply only through the verified portal at [meezanbank.com/careers](https://www.meezanbank.com/careers/).",
      "## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\n\n**Q1: Are fresh graduates eligible for these Meezan Bank roles?**\nNo. These specific vacancies are strictly reserved for candidates with prior banking experience (minimum 2 years for QA Analyst, 4 years for SBSO, and 5 years for Operation Manager). Fresh graduates should monitor Meezan Bank's entry-level Teller or Trainee intakes.\n\n**Q2: What is the application closing date?**\nThe deadline for **Operation Manager** and **Senior Branch Services Officer** is **05 November 2026**. The deadline for the **Quality Assurance Analyst** vacancy is **15 November 2026**.\n\n**Q3: Can candidates from conventional commercial banks apply?**\nYes. Experienced banking personnel from conventional banks are welcome to apply, provided they demonstrate willingness to adhere strictly to Shariah-compliant banking standards and Islamic banking regulations.\n\n**Q4: Where will the Quality Assurance Analyst be based?**\nThe Quality Assurance Analyst position is stationed permanently at Meezan Bank's Head Office in **Karachi**.",
      "## Official Links & Internal CareerDost Resources\n\n- **Official Career Portal:** [Meezan Bank Limited Job Portal](https://www.meezanbank.com/careers/)\n- **Related CareerDost Resources:**\n  - [Askari Bank Jobs October 2026 Karachi: Branch Manager & Operations](https://careerdost.blog/jobs/askari-bank-jobs-october-2026-karachi)\n  - [Bank Alfalah Jobs & Internships 2026: Counter Service Officer Guide](https://careerdost.blog/jobs/bank-alfalah-jobs-internships-2026)\n  - [HBL Careers 2026: The League Management Trainee Guide](https://careerdost.blog/jobs/hbl-jobs-internships-the-league-2026)\n  - [MCB Bank Jobs 2026: Information Security Trainee](https://careerdost.blog/jobs/mcb-bank-infosec-trainee-jobs-2026)"
